# AGENT CAPSULE

Bash hooks + local HANDOFF memory. One model per conversation.
Read `HANDOFF.md` for multi-session work. Prefer NO CODE. Smallest Diff. Zero prose comments.
Start: read HANDOFF.md tail. Stop with tools: update HANDOFF.
Git only when asked. Secrets never in code or chat.
Done = `docs/TOOLCHAIN.md` green with evidence.
Never fight a deny. Never reintroduce Rust kleos-gate or pack Python.

## Harness

Bash hooks: `session_start` (`additional_context`), `before_submit_prompt` (`continue` + JOB CARD nudge), `post_tool_use` (`additional_context` scorecard), `stop_gate` (`followup_message`), `lean_gate`/`pre_tool_use`/`before_shell`/`before_read_file`/`before_mcp` (`permission`). No Rust.
Brain = `HANDOFF.md` (local). Cloud agents: thin project hooks via `fleet_sync.sh project-hooks` (no sessionStart — avoids double DUTY).
Injection != Declaration: `sessionStart` injects `additional_context` only; `beforeSubmitPrompt` is continue/block. Never `updated_input`.

## INTENT protocol

Order: **GROUND → DECLARE → WRITE**. Grep/Glob/Read THIS codebase for the user's request first. Do not invent paths. Then declare `INTENT:` as chat prose before Write (never Shell/code-fence — poisons stop detection). Tags come from hits only.
Job card: `OBJECTIVE` = postcondition on named units (what is true when done — not implement/add/fix the…); `edit:path`|`NEW:path` from hits; `CONSTRAINTS` ≤2 invariants; `Done-when` ≤5 decidable predicates.

## File map

Ground → tag → edit/NEW → re-Read → prove Done-when.
Glob/Grep/Read first; `Write` for create/overwrite (Cursor primary write tool). pre_tool_use denies Write/Delete on a path that was not Read this session (NEW files need Grep/Glob first).
Finish EVERY tagged path this turn — no drip, no orphan unconnected files.
Before Done: verify all Done-when predicates with TOOLCHAIN evidence — cite green `bash tests/run.sh` / `scripts/doctor.sh` / package test in chat (stop_gate may soft-followup once if missing).

## State

`/state/` overwrite-only; clears on stop_gate success.
`pending_files.md` survives stop followups until accept.
Law: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` + `docs/CURATOR.md`.

## Autonomous loop (no early stops)

1. GROUND FIRST: Grep/Glob/Read this codebase for the user's request. Do not invent paths.
2. THEN DECLARE: INTENT in chat before Write (never Shell/fence). Tags from hits only.
3. NO ASK INSIDE INTENT: missing Done-when work → do it now.
4. NO PARTIAL HANDOFFS / NO DRIP.
5. WRITE: Write/StrReplace only tagged paths; cascade-fix.
6. PRE-STOP: re-Read tagged FILES; run TOOLCHAIN verify; cite green; prove Done-when; then `Done-when: met`.
7. CLOSE: stop_gate reads assistant prose from `transcript_path` and followups on poison/drip/unmet predicates / missing verify cite (fail-open after one nudge).
